2. How can you filter out all odd numbers from a list using list comprehension? Assume list `numbers`.
   A) [x for x in numbers if x % 2 == 0]
   B) [x for x in numbers if x % 2]
   C) [x for x in numbers if not x % 2]
   D) [x for x in numbers if x % 2 != 0]

3. Which list comprehension includes elements squared only if they are odd from the list [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]?
